# p_9c2d — Cycling commute, light dinner at the dining table only at 19:00 (fork of p_a1b2)

Fork of p_a1b2. The parent's plate claim ("Plates are at the dining table during dinner on weekdays, 18–19.5h") has accumulated 9 against-tallies. The 18:00 pass shows plate_yuki in the cupboard, and the 19:00 pass splits three ways (sink, dining table, cupboard). The plates are NOT at the dining table for the full 18:00–19:30 window; they appear there only briefly around 19:00–19:30, and even then only sometimes. The dinner is a light affair: plates are pulled from the cupboard, used at the dining table for about 30 minutes, then washed and returned. The 18:00 pass catches the kitchen before the plates are set out.

What changed: the class:plate dinner block is narrowed to 19.0–19.5h with "sometimes" (not "usually" or "almost_always"); the claim now targets the 19:00–19:5h window specifically; the 18:00–19:00 window has no plate-at-table prediction (plates stay in the cupboard). The cycling-commute structure (Yuki out 7.8–17.5, Omar out 13.7–23) is unchanged.

